krusty-toolchain compiles against the JDK `JAVA_HOME` names (a JDK 25 here) and provisions none:
a module that needs another version, always provisions, or picks a distribution is refused.
--- task
:app:compileJvm
--- project.yaml
modules:
  - app
  - older
  - provisioned
  - vendor
--- app/module.yaml
product: jvm/app
repositories:
  - mavenLocal
dependencies:
  - ../older
  - ../provisioned
  - ../vendor
--- app/src/main.kt
fun main() = Unit
--- older/module.yaml
product: jvm/lib
repositories:
  - mavenLocal
settings:
  jvm:
    jdk:
      version: 21
--- older/src/Older.kt
class Older
--- provisioned/module.yaml
product: jvm/lib
repositories:
  - mavenLocal
settings:
  jvm:
    jdk:
      selectionMode: alwaysProvision
--- provisioned/src/Provisioned.kt
class Provisioned
--- vendor/module.yaml
product: jvm/lib
repositories:
  - mavenLocal
settings:
  jvm:
    jdk:
      distributions:
        - temurin
--- vendor/src/Vendor.kt
class Vendor
--- krusty-refusal
error	older/module.yaml:7:16: ERROR: module `older` compiles against JDK 21, but JAVA_HOME (<directory>/jdk) is JDK 25, and krusty-toolchain does not provision JDKs
error	provisioned/module.yaml:7:22: ERROR: module `provisioned` sets `settings.jvm.jdk.selectionMode: alwaysProvision`, and krusty-toolchain does not provision JDKs
error	vendor/module.yaml:8:9: ERROR: module `vendor` sets `settings.jvm.jdk.distributions`, and krusty-toolchain does not check a JDK's distribution
